    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2024/04/saucony-endorphin-pro-4-review-2024.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The ride is highly cushioned and bouncy with a slight firm edge from the PWRRUN HG top layer; heel landings are smooth via a decent bevel, while the forefoot feels slightly stiff with a later rocker.",
        "Responsiveness: Energy return is strong at tempo to marathon efforts with noticeable bounce, but it is less snappy at top-end speeds and harder to push much faster than roughly 10K pace.",
        "Stability: The shoe feels stable through the platform, sole flare, and slightly stiff midfoot/forefoot transition; despite a thin/minimal heel counter, lockdown is secure when laced and heel slip was not reported.",
        "Durability: The review’s checklist rates durability expectation as above average, with no specific outsole wear or upper material breakdown issues cited in the provided excerpt."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2024/02/saucony-endorphin-pro-4-multi-tester.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The ride is described as soft, plush, and very cushioned with forgiving impact protection, giving a comfortable heel/forefoot feel without turning mushy.",
        "Responsiveness: Results are mixed—some testers found it snappy/bouncy, but others said it is less responsive with a less aggressive rocker and not as fast at shorter distances unless you land quickly on the forefoot.",
        "Stability: Stability is improved by a much wider midfoot platform (75 mm vs 67 mm in v3), plus secure lockdown and supportive heel/midfoot structure.",
        "Durability: Long-term outsole wear is not yet reported, but the updated outsole improved wet-road performance and the revised upper/toe-bumper design is expected to improve material longevity versus v3 (which tore around 300 miles)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/saucony-endorphin-pro-4-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The PWRRUN PB/HG setup feels soft and comfortable on step-in, is slightly softer than Pro 3, and adds impact protection without feeling harsh, with a smooth heel-to-toe transition.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride is repeatedly described as snappy, bouncy, and propulsive, with strong pop from the carbon plate + Speedroll combo and better energy return at faster paces.",
        "Stability: Reviewers noted improved underfoot stability versus the prior model, secure fit from the upper/heel structure, and the ability to run slower paces without feeling unstable.",
        "Durability: With 75+ miles on test pairs, no major durability issues were called out; the lattice outsole was reported to work well, indicating solid short-to-mid-term outsole/material longevity."
      ]
    }
